{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "notes": [
    "Which way the chat reads a message (chat.graph.decide_intent): the message, the situation it arrives in and the intent a sensible person would call it. The rules decide; nothing is planned and no model is called.",
    "Situations: none = nothing planned yet; route = a route with two alternatives is on screen; asking = the step-by-step dialogue waits for an answer; failed = the last request found no route.",
    "'expected' is what the chat SHOULD do, not what the rules happen to do. The cases the rules get wrong are the point: they are where a better reader (more rules, or a model behind them) has to improve, and a rule change must not lose the others.",
    "plan_text cases assume a configured language-model parser (the runner's text_enabled=True); without one, free text goes to the question-and-answer dialogue.",
    "New cases come from real messages: 'bike-router chat misses --export-cases' lists the ones the chat could not read; a person labels 'expected' and adds them."
  ],
